---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ResponsiveImage from '../../components/ResponsiveImage.astro';
import { about, pillars } from '../../data/gallery.js';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Trevor Ludwyck is a photographer based in Celina, TX, working throughout Dallas–Fort Worth. Oklahoma-raised, Oklahoma State journalism grad, and full-time staff at Shoreline City Church."
>
  <section class="about wrap">
    <div class="about__image">
      <ResponsiveImage src={about.src} alt={about.alt} sizes="(min-width: 900px) 40vw, 100vw" />
    </div>
    <div class="about__content">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Less is more.</h1>
      <p>
        I was born and raised in Oklahoma, where I first picked up a camera
        young, photographing wildlife on hunting trips with my dad.
      </p>
      <p>
        I studied journalism at Oklahoma State University, where I met my
        wife. We now live in Celina, TX, where I'm on staff full-time at our
        church, Shoreline City.
      </p>
      <p>
        To me, photography is about freezing a single moment in time, and
        using it to tell the story of who someone is and what they love.
        That philosophy shapes my approach: simple, deliberate, and built on
        the belief that real skill shows up as efficiency, not excess.
      </p>
      <a href="/contact/" class="btn">Inquire</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pillars wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Philosophy</p>
    <h2>My Three Pillars</h2>
    <p class="pillars__intro">
      Vision changes how you approach everything — including a camera.
      These are the three ideas that shape the way I see, and the way I
      shoot.
    </p>

    <div class="pillars__list">
      <details class="pillar">
        <summary class="pillar__summary">
          <span class="pillar__name">Light</span>
          <span class="pillar__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="pillar__content">
          <ResponsiveImage
            src={pillars.light.src}
            alt={pillars.light.alt}
            sizes="(min-width: 700px) 500px, 100vw"
            class="pillar__image"
          />
          <div class="pillar__text">
            <p class="pillar__verse">
              Genesis 1:3 — "And God said, 'Let there be light,' and there
              was light."
            </p>
            <p>
              Light is the first thing God ever created — and it's the
              first thing I think about on every session. Photography was
              never really about capturing photos to me. It's about
              capturing and shaping light to narrate the story I'm trying
              to tell.
            </p>
            <p>
              Where the light falls, what it reveals, what it leaves in
              shadow — that's the actual craft. The camera, the lens, the
              location: all of it just serves the light.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="pillar">
        <summary class="pillar__summary">
          <span class="pillar__name">Contrast</span>
          <span class="pillar__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="pillar__content">
          <ResponsiveImage
            src={pillars.contrast.src}
            alt={pillars.contrast.alt}
            sizes="(min-width: 700px) 500px, 100vw"
            class={pillars.contrast.grayscale ? 'pillar__image pillar__image--grayscale' : 'pillar__image'}
          />
          <div class="pillar__text">
            <p>
              Contrast is the ingredient behind anything that's genuinely
              good. A painting needs light against dark to have depth. A
              dish needs something acidic against something rich, or sweet
              against salt, to actually taste like anything. A scent falls
              flat without a top note working against a base note.
            </p>
            <p>
              Photography runs on the same rule. Without contrast — in
              light, in tone, in composition — an image goes flat too.
              Contrast is what gives a photograph depth, weight, and a
              reason to look twice.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="pillar">
        <summary class="pillar__summary">
          <span class="pillar__name">Simplicity</span>
          <span class="pillar__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="pillar__content">
          <ResponsiveImage
            src={pillars.simplicity.src}
            alt={pillars.simplicity.alt}
            sizes="(min-width: 700px) 500px, 100vw"
            class="pillar__image"
          />
          <div class="pillar__text">
            <p>
              I believe true skill is found in finishing a task the
              easiest, most efficient way possible — not in making the
              task itself easy. Take CrossFit: the best athletes in the
              world aren't the best because they've figured out how to
              make CrossFit easy. They've found the most efficient way to
              do something that's still genuinely hard.
            </p>
            <p>
              It's the same behind a camera. Less is always more — fewer
              props, fewer poses, fewer distractions. The skill was never
              in the complexity. It's in knowing exactly what to leave
              out.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: calc(var(--space-xl) + 2rem) var(--space-xl);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5fr 7fr;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .about__image :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .about__content h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4.5vw, 3rem);
    margin-block: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
  }

  .about__content p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    max-width: 58ch;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .about__content .btn {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .about {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .pillars {
    padding-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .pillars h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.85rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    margin-block: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
  }

  .pillars__intro {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .pillars__list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .pillar {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .pillar__summary {
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    padding-block: var(--space-md);
  }

  .pillar__summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .pillar__summary::marker {
    content: '';
  }

  .pillar__name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.5vw, 2.25rem);
  }

  .pillar__icon {
    position: relative;
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .pillar__icon::before,
  .pillar__icon::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    background: var(--color-gold);
  }

  .pillar__icon::before {
    top: 50%;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 1px;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
  }

  .pillar__icon::after {
    left: 50%;
    top: 0;
    width: 1px;
    height: 100%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
  }

  details[open] .pillar__icon::after {
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .pillar__content {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5fr 7fr;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    align-items: start;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .pillar__content :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .pillar__content :global(img.pillar__image--grayscale) {
    filter: grayscale(1);
  }

  .pillar__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .pillar__verse {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-gold);
    padding-left: var(--space-sm);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .pillar__content {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
